  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Cultural Mediation Support to the International Protection Office (IPO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Built on the initial successful results of the &#x201C;Registration of the Ukrainian nationals and TCNs from Ukraine entering Ireland&#x201D; Project led by IOM Ireland in support of the Department of Justice (DOJ) in the framework of the Ukrainian crisis response, started in March 2022, the project is designed to support the International Protection Office (IPO) in Dublin, part of DOJ, through the deployment of a trained pool of cultural mediators (CMs). Upon direct request to IOM, the IPO would like to explore further sustainable collaboration with IOM, regarding the facilitation and systematization of the interview phase, part of the procedure for the International Protection application.</narrative>
  </description>
